  "rule": "Corner legends (solid frames of colour C containing tail->2 arrows) each fix one of 8 directions. Lift every 4-marker. Each marker slides in the direction of the legend whose colour matches its enclosing outline. It moves while the next cell is background, and a diagonal step is refused if either orthogonal side cell is a wall. All slides are computed on the lifted grid, and the markers are then redrawn at their end cells.",
  "scope": "Decode corner arrow legends and slide markers inside corresponding coloured outlines, including diagonal corner guards, touching outlines, preserved interior pillars and actual outline-wall markers.",
  "constraints": [
    "Fixed wall-marker selection to draw candidates only from the outline ring while retaining pillars as obstacles; original code consumed pillar cells in 24/80 forced trials and removed every pillar in 2/80. Repaired 80/80 controls retained all pillars and had an actual outline marker.",
    "Independent input-only legend, region and ray-prefix verification passed 1160 distinct scenes containing 5577 markers and 496 corner-guard stops, spanning all eight directions.",
    "Forty 16x16 diagonal-wall cases without pillars and forty 30x30 multicolour/touching/pillar/wall-marker combinations succeeded.",
    "Explicit replay now requires nonempty markers and rejects a marker starting on another path; all five canonical fixtures remain exact.",
    "Unhashable colour entries reject as ValueError after type validation precedes distinctness checking.",
    "Documented two-outline cap below 500 cells and same-colour touching/shared-wall semantics.",
    "Final parameter retest: 30 successes and six expected rejections, no overrides."
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "Each generated marker region has one bordering legend colour; multi-colour border-majority inference is not exercised.",
    "Original hand-drawn outlines are replayed from explicit layouts; procedural scenes use unions of rectangles and staircases.",
    "Explicit replay trusts supplied legend direction, but rejects absent markers, unmoving markers, duplicate endpoints and starts on another marker's path.",
    "Under 500 cells there are at most two outlines per colour; larger canvases allow three subject to packing.",
    "Non-20x20 sizes and optional shape/control combinations are synthetic extensions."
  ],
